(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "cloud-itonami-isic-5811 book-publishing operations-coordination actor implementation" "fresh scaffold closing the kotoba-lang/industry :spec entry gap for ISIC 5811")), (:adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-5811-book-publishing-coverage"), (:adr/related (vector "cloud-itonami-isic-873" "ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2616581100-cloud-itonami-isic-5811-book-publishing-coverage"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-16"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2616581100: cloud-itonami-isic-5811 (Book publishing) book-publishing operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)\n**Related**: ADR-2607121000 (Wave 3, production/robotics), ADR-2607152500\n(Wave 4, human-facing/personal services -- authorizes this batch to\nproceed in parallel with Wave 3), cloud-itonami-isic-873 (Residential\ncare for elderly/disabled -- the Wave 4 flagship reference module shape\nthis actor mirrors, independently re-read in full before use), the\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry's `\"5811\"` catalog entry\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry carried a `\"5811\"` entry at\n`:maturity :spec` with `:name \"Book publishing\"` (matching the assigned\nISIC class, verified via fresh clone before any work began) and\n`:repo \"https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5811\"` (an old,\nnever-populated naming scheme). Confirmed no repo exists yet at either\nthat stale placeholder or the real `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5811`\ntarget (`gh api` 404 for the latter) before any work began. A separate,\nredundant 3-digit group entry `{:id \"581\" ...}` also exists at\n`:maturity :spec` with a truncated `:name` field ending in `\"...\"` --\nthis is a known, pre-existing seed-data artifact from an earlier\ndata-seeding pass, distinct from the `\"5811\"` class-level entry, and was\ndeliberately NOT touched or promoted by this change.\n\nThis is part of Wave 4 (human-facing/personal-services fleet,\nISIC sections I/P/Q/R/S/T), running in parallel with the ongoing Wave 3\n(production/robotics) rollout per ADR-2607152500. Book publishing\ntouches editorial/content-decision authority and rights/licensing\ndecisions, so this actor is deliberately scoped to back-office\noperations coordination only, with a closed op allowlist that\nstructurally excludes finalizing an editorial-content decision, a\ndefamation/legal-risk clearance decision, and a rights/licensing grant\ndecision -- those remain exclusively human/institutional decisions,\nnever an auto-commit-eligible op, per Wave 4's person-facing-service\nsafety guardrail.\n\n## Decision\n\nScaffold `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5811` as a book-publishing\nOPERATIONS COORDINATION actor (not editorial-content-decision authority,\nnot a legal-risk-clearance authority, not a rights/licensing-grant\nauthority), mirroring `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s verified module shape\n(`store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`phase`/`operation`/`sim`,\n`deps.edn`/`blueprint.edn`/README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/\nCONTRIBUTING/SECURITY, AGPL-3.0-or-later) with fresh, book-publishing-\nspecific domain logic under the `bookpubops` namespace:\n\n1. **`bookpubops.store`** -- `MemStore` (atom of EDN) behind a `Store`\n   protocol; a `titles` directory keyed by `:title-id` STRING (a book\n   title under contract with the publishing house), plus an\n   append-only `ledger` and a `coordination-log` of committed records.\n2. **`bookpubops.advisor`** (\"BookPubAdvisor\") -- deterministic mock\n   advisor drafting exactly four kinds of proposal: production-record\n   logging (manuscript/print-run/ISBN-assignment data),\n   production-operation scheduling (editing/typesetting/print-run\n   scheduling), distribution coordination (outbound print-run/ebook\n   distribution), and content-concern flagging (defamation/copyright/\n   factual-accuracy risk). Every proposal's `:effect` is always\n   `:propose`; every output is censored downstream by the governor.\n3. **`bookpubops.governor`** (\"BookPubGovernor\") -- three HARD checks,\n   all permanent and un-overridable: (1) title-unverified -- the\n   target title record must exist AND be independently\n   `:registered?`/`:verified?` in the store before ANY proposal for it\n   may commit or escalate; (2) effect-not-propose -- any `:effect`\n   other than `:propose` is HARD-blocked; (3) scope-exclusion -- any\n   proposal (regardless of op) whose op/summary/rationale/cites/value\n   touches finalizing-an-editorial-content-decision,\n   legal-risk-clearance, or rights/licensing-grant territory is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block, unconditionally evaluated on every proposal; an op\n   outside the closed four-op allowlist is folded into this same check.\n   One ESCALATE (soft) gate: `:flag-content-concern` ALWAYS escalates\n   to a human regardless of confidence, as does low confidence\n   generally.\n4. **`bookpubops.phase`** -- Phase 0->3 staged rollout;\n   `:flag-content-concern` is permanently ABSENT from every phase's\n   `:auto` set (structural fact, not a rollout milestone still to\n   come) -- only `:log-production-record`/`:schedule-production-\n   operation`/`:coordinate-distribution` may auto-commit at phase 3\n   when governor-clean.\n5. **`bookpubops.operation`** (\"OperationActor\") -- langgraph-clj\n   StateGraph, `intake -> advise -> govern -> decide -> commit | hold |\n   request-approval`, `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` for\n   human-in-the-loop sign-off, invoked exclusively via\n   `langgraph.graph/run*`.\n6. **`deps.edn` / `blueprint.edn` / docs** -- mirror\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s shape (`:test`/`:lint`/`:run`/`:dev`\n   aliases pinned to the same `kotoba-lang/langgraph` git SHA\n   `a332a770a0d2b5193f81b54483bb954fb29ef8d7`, `itonami.blueprint/*`\n   metadata, scope/design/testing README sections).\n\n### What this actor does NOT do\n\nFinalizing an editorial-content decision (what the book actually says,\nwhether it ships as written), issuing a defamation/legal-risk\nclearance decision, and granting rights or licensing terms to an\nauthor, translator, distributor, or any other party all remain\nexclusively human/institutional decisions, permanently, with no actor\nor human-approval override path -- enforced structurally by the\ngovernor's closed op/effect allowlists and the unconditional\nscope-exclusion check, not just documented. `:flag-content-concern` is\na \"surface the concern\" op only; it can never self-clear the concern it\nraises, and is never a member of any phase's `:auto` set.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5811`: `clojure -M:test` -- raw final line: `Ran\n  44 tests containing 122 assertions.` / `0 failures, 0 errors.`\n  (re-run green a second time from a brand-new fresh clone after push).\n- `clojure -M:lint` -- 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `clojure -M:run` demo narrative exercises proposal submission,\n  escalation/approval on every write op, and every HARD-hold scenario\n  directly (unregistered title, unverified title, non-`:propose`\n  effect, editorial-content/legal-clearance/rights-grant scope drift)\n  -- ran clean, no exceptions.\n- A dedicated regression test\n  (`default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion` in\n  `test/bookpubops/advisor_test.clj`) independently confirms every op's\n  own default (clean) advisor-generated proposal text clears the\n  governor's scope-exclusion scan -- catching, during development, an\n  early draft bug where the `coordinate-distribution` advisor's own\n  disclaimer text (\"no rights-licensing judgment included\") happened to\n  contain the literal excluded term itself and so self-tripped a HARD\n  block on every clean proposal; fixed by rewording the disclaimer.\n- All source under `src/`/`test/` is `.cljc`, no JVM-only interop; the\n  actor graph is invoked exclusively via `langgraph.graph/run*`.\n- Repo created fresh (`gh repo create` + push, public visibility\n  matching the reference and `blueprint.edn`'s `:status :public-oss`),\n  initial commit `3c76aa0` on `cloud-itonami-isic-5811`'s `main` (no\n  prior history), confirmed via a brand-new fresh clone.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"5811\"` entry updated in place\n  (exact-text edit of the literal `{:id \"5811\" ...}` block only, no\n  other entry's block touched, and the separate `\"581\"` group entry\n  left untouched, byte-offset-diff-verified confined to the intended\n  region): `:repo`/`:business-id` corrected from the never-populated\n  `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5811` naming to `cloud-itonami/cloud-\n  itonami-isic-5811` / `cloud-itonami-isic-5811`, `:required-\n  technologies` normalized from a stale `[:robotics :identity :forms\n  :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :phone]` placeholder to the coordination-\n  only shape actually implemented `[:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn\n  :audit-ledger]` (matching sibling `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s own\n  `:required-technologies`), `:maturity` `:spec` -> `:implemented`;\n  `:name` was already the full, correct \"Book publishing\" (not\n  affected by the ~10%-of-entries truncated-name seed-data bug, so no\n  de-truncation was needed). Landed via a Contents API single-file PUT\n  (sha-checked optimistic concurrency; the first two sha checks\n  drifted from concurrent sibling registry edits before the third\n  attempt's PUT succeeded), commit `89a816e6a6b49ddcb60465ae37324024344fdf43`.\n- `test/kotoba/industry_test.clj`'s `maturity-summary` assertion\n  bumped, live-recomputed via `(kotoba.industry/maturity-summary)`\n  against freshly re-fetched content immediately before each PUT\n  attempt (never a reused/stale buffer) -- this file is an extremely\n  hot, high-concurrency shared file across the fleet, and this\n  promotion's own testing block landed via commit\n  `504ef60ac8e1fbb5a4975ede84516ff45b2792c9`. **Transparency note**: a\n  bug in this agent's own bounded-retry helper script (a stale\n  off-by-one regex plus a race between two separate fetches -- the\n  registry-derived count and the test-file's already-landed count --\n  meaning the script used a stale, lower count instead of the file's\n  own already-more-current value) caused that same commit to\n  transiently *regress* the final count assertion from a\n  concurrently-landed `377` down to `376`. This was caught during this\n  agent's own post-landing re-verification (re-fetching and\n  recomputing the true live count via the real\n  `kotoba.industry/maturity-summary` function, not the buggy script's\n  logic) and a corrective fix was in flight when a concurrent sibling\n  agent's own independent fleet-drift correction (commit\n  `c1df84a4da90...`, \"test: fix implemented-count assertion 376 -> 378\n  (concurrent fleet drift)\") landed first and corrected it to the true\n  live value `378`, confirmed matching a fresh\n  `(kotoba.industry/maturity-summary)` recompute. Net effect: correct,\n  but only because of this agent's own re-verification catching the\n  regression plus a concurrent sibling's independent correction landing\n  before this agent's own corrective PUT was needed -- documented here\n  in full rather than omitted, per this fleet's honest-reporting norm.\n- Full `kotoba-lang/industry` suite re-run green after all edits (fresh\n  clone, plus a fresh `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling clone for\n  `deps.edn` resolution): `Ran 15 tests containing 1040 assertions.` /\n  `0 failures, 0 errors.`\n- Final post-merge re-verification (brand-new scratch directory, fresh\n  `origin/main` clone of both `cloud-itonami-isic-5811` and\n  `kotoba-lang/industry`, plus a fresh `kotoba-lang/technology`\n  sibling): `clojure -M:test` re-run green in both repos; the\n  registry's `\"5811\"` entry confirmed `:maturity :implemented` with the\n  corrected `:repo`/`:business-id`/`:required-technologies`, and a\n  sample of sibling entries (`873`/`6310`/`581`/`2513`/`5630`)\n  confirmed untouched. `grep -c` for the UTF-8 replacement character\n  against `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` returned `0` (no\n  file-wide mojibake).\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) `cloud-itonami-isic-5811` now has a real, tested implementation\nmatching the shape of every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor, replacing a\n`:spec` placeholder pointing at a repo that never existed.\n\n(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"5811\"` entry promoted to\n`:maturity :implemented`.\n\n(+) This actor is a second concrete example (after `cloud-itonami-isic-\n873`) of Wave 4's person-facing-service safety guardrail applied to a\ndifferent sensitive-decision axis: instead of clinical/care-authority\nexclusions, this actor structurally excludes editorial-content-decision,\nlegal-risk-clearance, and rights/licensing-grant authority, all folded\ninto one unconditional scope-exclusion check that never trusts the\nadvisor's own framing of its intent.\n\n(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer, not a real publishing-operations\nsystem. Editorial decisions, legal clearance, and rights/licensing\ngrants remain human-/institution-controlled via external channels.\n\n(-) No integration with real publishing-house systems (manuscript\nmanagement, print-run scheduling, ISBN registries, rights/licensing\ndatabases, distribution partner APIs) -- this is a standalone\ncoordinator blueprint, matching every prior sibling actor's own stated\nlimitation."), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-16"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2616581100: cloud-itonami-isic-5811 (Book publishing) book-publishing operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))